# Mandos — example secrets file.
#
# The configurator writes real secrets to `~/.mandos/.env` (0600). This file is
# illustrative: values are referenced by NAME from the config (api_key_env) and
# loaded into the environment at startup without overriding already-set vars.
# Local/subscription providers that need no key can be omitted.
# NEVER commit a real .env (plan §14).

# The Jev judge's key. Which one is read follows `judge.provider`, so both can sit
# here at once and only the relevant one is used.
TYPESAFE_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Panel providers.
MINIMAX_API_KEY=
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# Optional: point the server at a specific config file.
# MANDOS_CONFIG=/etc/mandos/config.json
